12
00:58:57,391 --> 00:59:03,391
Confessions of a Dangerous Mind is a 2002 American biographical spy film directed by
George Clooney in his directorial debut and written by Charlie Kaufman.

13
01:03:52,173 --> 01:03:58,173
It stars Sam Rockwell as game show host and producer Chuck Barris; based on Barris' 1984 "unauthorized autobiography" of the same name, in which he makes unsubstantiated
claims to have worked for the CIA, it also depicts Barris' alleged second career as an international assassin, albeit in an over-the-top, absurdist manner.

14
01:08:46,956 --> 01:08:52,956
Drew Barrymore, Clooney, Julia Roberts and Rutger
Hauer star in supporting roles.

15
01:13:41,739 --> 01:13:47,739
The film had a long development process; Columbia Pictures first planned to produce a film adaptation of the
autobiography in the late 1980s, to be directed by Jim McBride, although nothing came of it.

16
01:18:36,521 --> 01:18:42,521
The film rights were purchased in 1997 by producer Andrew Lazar, who hired Kaufman to write a screenplay that quickly attracted a string of well-known
directors, including David Fincher, Brian De Palma and Bryan Singer, and actors, including Mike Myers, Ben Stiller and Johnny Depp.

17
01:23:31,304 --> 01:23:37,304
When Clooney was hired to direct, he championed the casting of the then-unknown Rockwell and brought on Barris as consultant to provide additional
authenticity; this led to uncredited rewrites that left Kaufman unhappy with the final result, including the removal of a drug addiction subplot.

18
01:28:26,086 --> 01:28:32,086
To accommodate the $30 million budget, Clooney convinced
Barrymore and Roberts to lower their salaries.

19
01:33:20,869 --> 01:33:26,869
The film was released theatrically in the United States on
December 31, 2002, performing poorly at the box office.

20
01:38:15,652 --> 01:38:21,652
However, it received favorable reviews from critics, who praised its performances, in particular that of
Rockwell, who won the Silver Bear for Best Actor at the 2003 Berlin International Film Festival.

21
01:43:10,434 --> 01:43:16,434
The film explores themes of regret, double life,
assassination, based on novel or book, hitman.

22
01:48:05,217 --> 01:48:11,217
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
